{
  "version": 1,
  "story": "phase 0 story 1 (what is due today and project status with citations); phase 1 stories 2 and 3 (enter labor numbers, create a project) plus a to-do; phase 2 story 4 (split bid files); phase 3 story 5 (a 7 AM recurring report and stop sending it) plus memory; phase 4 stories P, E, R and W plus PM, certified payroll, memory_search, find_tools and three refusals",
  "notes": "Every scenario runs against the dev Supabase project on the TS-* seed projects (tests/../scratch/seed_staging_analytics.py shapes), never BDR_Prod. expected.tools lists the tools a correct answer calls (order-free); expected.cites lists project numbers the answer must contain; expected.must_not lists substrings the answer must not contain. Phase 1: expected.approvals lists the approval cards a turn must end with ({tool, rows: {field: substring of the row's after text}}); expected.no_approval asserts the turn made no card. The runner rejects every card still pending at the end of each case, so no eval writes. Phase 3: seed_schedules creates routines before the message (ended at cleanup); memory true sends the message without Incognito (every other message is Incognito, so the eval account's notes never change another case); expected.not_tools lists tools the turn must not call, expected.memory_saved the fields of a note the turn must save, and expected.seeded_status the status every seeded routine must end in. Every note a case saves is deleted at cleanup. Phase 4: {{ae01_*}}, {{est01_*}} and {{intake01_*}} name a dev project with a finished AI Estimating run, one with an estimator assignment and a test project whose intake lane sits at intake; a case whose fixture is missing on dev is skipped. expected.approvals_only lists the only tools a card may be for; expected.role_must_not lists substrings checked only when the eval account runs at the scenario's role. build_report writes the account's own spreadsheet (expires in 7 days); no card is ever approved.",
